kerrank-orchestrate-october26/output.csv))**:\n   - 518 evaluation rows, naturally sorted by `case_id`, passing all 12 contract assertions.\n4. **Packaged Archives**:\n   - **[`code.zip`](file:///home/skandan-c-y/PycharmProjects/hackerrank-orchestrate-october26/code.zip)** (cleanly packaged without dataset or cache files).\n   - **[`agent-trace.zip`](file:///home/skandan-c-y/PycharmProjects/hackerrank-orchestrate-october26/agent-trace.zip)** (staged conversation trace).\n   - **[`log.txt`](file:///home/skandan-c-y/PycharmProjects/hackerrank-orchestrate-october26/log.txt)** (append-only audit log with authoritative `tool` and `model` headers).\n\n---\n\n### What Remains for You to Do\n\n#### 1. Submit on HackerRank\nNavigate to the official challenge submission page:\n**https://www.hackerrank.com/contests/hackerrank-orchestrate-october26/challenges/ghost-data-still-exists**\n\nUpload the following files from your repository root:\n* **`code.zip`** $\\to$ Code submission slot.\n* **`output.csv`** $\\to$ Output predictions slot.\n* **`log.txt`** $\\to$ `chat_transcript` slot.\n* **`agent-trace.zip`** $\\to$ Agent trace slot (if prompted).\n\n#### 2. Prepare for the AI Interview (Cheat Sheet for C++ Devs)\nThe submission includes an AI interview explaining your architecture, investigation approach, remediation planning, and evaluation. Here is the concise mental model to keep in mind:\n\n- **Architecture**: A modular, four-stage deterministic pipeline:\n  1. *Intent Classification*: Differentiates Article 17 erasure requests from Article 15/16/20 access/rectification/portability requests (the latter yield `NOT_APPLICABLE` with `[]`).\n  2. *Identity Resolution*: Constructs a temporal identity graph from current snapshots and historical audit logs, deriving SHA-256 hashes of all email variations to catch pseudonymized records.\n  3. *Evidence Mining & Temporal Invariant*: Executes SQLite in-memory table reflection, correlates multi-line service logs by `trace_id`, and strictly ignores any evidence created after `audit_at`.\n  4. *Policy Engine*: Applies `deletion_rules.csv` to synthesize finding, remediation, and verification steps.\n- **Remediation Ordering (DAG)**:\n  - Upstream data flows (`DISABLE_DATA_FLOW`) and restore paths (`BLOCK_RESTORE`) are blocked *before* mutating or deleting records (`DELETE_RECORD`, `REDACT_RECORD`).\n  - Downstream read replicas and search indices are remediated in coordination with primary datastores to avoid replication resurrection.\n- **Account Tombstones**:\n  - For account tombstones, the stable `user_id` is preserved to maintain referential integrity, while all direct PII (name, email, phone, hashes) is redacted.\n- **Evaluation & Cost**:\n  - Validated against the 32 sample ground-truth cases (100% status and field accuracy).\n  - Evaluated on 3 custom synthetic edge cases (residual tombstone leaks, sync connector recreation, and statutory compliance holds).\n  - Total LLM API calls during evaluation: **0**. Cost: **$0.00**.","thinking":"Project engineering is complete, with code fully written, calibrated, and evaluated with successful root output. Reports and supporting archives are generated. The next step involves submission using the provided URL.\n\n\n"}
